10. MOST IMPORTANT FEATURE – INTELLIGENT FACTORY RECOVERY ENGINE

==================================================

This is the main innovation of FactoryPulse IntelliOps.

Do not implement this as a static page.

Build an actual working decision-support engine.

ROUTE:

/manager/recovery-engine

Purpose:

Identify the operational consequences of a machine fault, worker absence or production shortage and recommend suitable recovery options.

The system must use real database records.

10.1 Problem Detection

Support these events:

Machine fault.
Worker absence.
Production shortage.
Machine maintenance.
Sudden increase in production demand.

Events can originate from:

Worker reports.
Manager actions.
Maintenance reports.
Simulated operational scenarios.
10.2 Impact Identification

When a machine fault occurs, identify:

Affected machine.
Assigned workers.
Production orders.
Current production capacity.
Machine compatibility requirements.
Available alternative machines.
Available qualified workers.
10.3 Resource Allocation Engine

Implement a rule-based resource allocation algorithm.

Hard constraints:

Worker must be available.
Worker must possess the required skills.
Worker must have required certifications.
Machine must be operational.
Machine must support the production task.
Worker must not have conflicting assignments.
Shift requirements must be respected.

After enforcing hard constraints, calculate a recommendation score.

Suggested weights:

Skill compatibility: 35%.
Worker availability: 25%.
Machine compatibility: 20%.
Production priority: 10%.
Assignment efficiency: 10%.

Normalize scores to a 0–100 scale.

These weights should be configurable.

Never assign an ineligible worker simply because that worker has a high score.

10.4 Recovery Recommendation Interface

Display:

Incident summary.
Affected machine.
Affected workers.
Affected production orders.
Alternative machines.
Eligible workers.
Recommended assignments.
Recommendation scores.
Estimated production impact.

Provide three actions:

Approve.
Modify.
Reject.

The manager must always retain final approval authority.

10.5 Recovery Execution

After manager approval:

Validate the recovery plan again.
Check current worker availability.
Check machine status.
Check shift conflicts.
Update assignments in a database transaction.
Update production assignments.
Create an audit record.
Generate notifications.
Refresh relevant dashboards.
Save the recovery history.

If any required resource becomes unavailable before approval, reject the stale plan and recalculate it.

10.6 Recovery Comparison

Display a before-and-after comparison.

Metrics:

Active machines.
Available workers.
Assigned workers.
Production capacity.
Estimated production delay.
Resource utilization.

Use calculated values from the actual simulation.

Clearly distinguish measured historical information from estimated scenario outputs.

