→ Worker sees updated assignment.

WORKFLOW B:

Manager creates a production order.
→ Worker receives task assignment.
→ Worker updates production progress.
→ Manager sees updated production.
→ Analytics update.

WORKFLOW C:

Technician completes maintenance.
→ Machine status updates after authorized confirmation.
→ Manager sees machine availability.
→ Recovery engine can use the machine again.

WORKFLOW D:

Worker submits safety incident.
→ Manager sees incident.
→ Manager assigns corrective action.
→ Responsible person receives notification.
→ Incident status updates.
→ Safety analytics refresh.

Every workflow must use the same underlying database records.

